[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is this notion in Mathlib?<br>\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principal_root_of_unity\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principal_root_of_unity</a></p>",
        "id": 596052405,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1779164661
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This topic was moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Principal.20root.20of.20unity\">#mathlib4 &gt; Principal root of unity</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"238446\">Anne Baanen</span>.</p>",
        "id": 596087101,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1779177506
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We do have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsPrimitiveRoot#doc\">docs#IsPrimitiveRoot</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsPrimitiveRoot.geom_sum_eq_zero#doc\">docs#IsPrimitiveRoot.geom_sum_eq_zero</a> but I don't think we have principal roots as their own definition.</p>",
        "id": 596088488,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1779177741
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am pretty sure we don't have this, but we have <em>a lot</em> about roots of unity, so it shouldn't be a problem to prove everything you need.</p>",
        "id": 596090136,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779178214
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We have nice stuff, but I don't think mathlib even knows that the sum of roots of unity is zero, and other basic properties. This area needs work IMO.<br>\n(<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsPrimitiveRoot.geom_sum_eq_zero#doc\">docs#IsPrimitiveRoot.geom_sum_eq_zero</a> is the closest we have AFAIK)</p>",
        "id": 596196858,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779203107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sum of 1st roots of unity is 1 :-)</p>",
        "id": 596215016,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779206967
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>btw when <code>1 &lt; k</code> it works for <code>ℤ</code> <code>ℚ</code> <code>ℝ</code> <code>ℂ</code> but not for <code>ℕ</code>, and I have no idea if it generalizes.<br>\nFor <code>ZMod p</code> (<code>p</code> odd prime) it only works when <code>k</code> is even <span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span><br>\nPerhaps it works for any <code>CommRing</code> + <code>CharZero</code></p>",
        "id": 596237032,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779210983
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>See <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Sum.20of.20N-th.20roots.20of.20unity/with/585108243\">this</a> recent discussion. Note that the PR I opended is now merged.</p>",
        "id": 596237545,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1779211105
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Principal.20root.20of.20unity/near/596237032\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For <code>ZMod p</code> (<code>p</code> odd prime) it only works when <code>k</code> is even <span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>What do you mean by this?</p>",
        "id": 596238951,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779211490
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Principal.20root.20of.20unity/near/596238951\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Principal.20root.20of.20unity/near/596237032\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For <code>ZMod p</code> (<code>p</code> odd prime) it only works when <code>k</code> is even <span aria-label=\"shrug\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f937\" role=\"img\" title=\"shrug\">:shrug:</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>What do you mean by this?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n<p>code</p>\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rootsOfUnity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ζ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ζ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subtype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">rootsOfUnity</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_mk</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_mk</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subsemigroup</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_mk</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">infer_instance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prime</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∑</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rootsOfUnity</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">val</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>\n<p>and e.g. the sum of 3rd roots-of-unity in <code>ZMod 11</code> is 1 and not 0.<br>\nAFAICT in <code>ZMod p</code> (<code>p</code> prime) the sum of <code>k</code>th roots-of-unity is 0 iff there's a <code>k</code>th root-of-unity other than 1.</p>",
        "id": 596244845,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779213129
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>well, in <code>ℝ</code> too, the sum of the third roots of unity is one and not zero</p>",
        "id": 596246408,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779213569
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>since the only cube root of unity is <code>1</code></p>",
        "id": 596246504,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779213601
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right, whoops. So basically for any <code>CommMonoidWithZero</code> + <code>NoZeroDivisors</code> that I've tried (which isn't a lot), the sum is zero iff there's more than one root. idk what the correct hypotheses are though.<br>\n(I do know that if a <em>primitive</em> root exists which isn't 1, the sum is zero given <code>CommRing</code> <code>IsDomain</code>)</p>",
        "id": 596249380,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1779214321
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can't do addition in a <code>CommMonoidWithZero</code>. The moment there's some <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> th root <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\zeta\\not=1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0738em;\">ζ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mord vbox\"><span class=\"thinbox\"><span class=\"rlap\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"inner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"></span></span></span><span class=\"fix\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> then multiplication by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\zeta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0738em;\">ζ</span></span></span></span> is a bijection from the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span> th roots to themselves, so if <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> is the sum then <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1-\\zeta)S=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0738em;\">ζ</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> meaning <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> if there are no zero divisors.</p>",
        "id": 596299231,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1779229463
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>that proof works for semirings too, right? can we generalize the version in mathlib to semirings</p>",
        "id": 596301548,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779230533
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh it looks like there's actually almost no material on primitive roots in semirings</p>",
        "id": 596302017,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779230770
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>wait actually you don't even need a primitive root of unity for that you just need a root of unity that's not <code>1</code></p>",
        "id": 596302320,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1779230922
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for your comments!  I continued the discussion in the thread that <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130384\">@Riccardo Brasca</span> pointed to above:<br>\n<a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"217875\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Sum.20of.20N-th.20roots.20of.20unity/with/596336830\">#Is there code for X? &gt; Sum of N-th roots of unity</a></p>",
        "id": 596336944,
